      "message": "This approach makes sense semantically, but technically a null pointer dereference is undefined behavior -- so the compiler assumes that references are always non-null, and will likely not do what you expect below.\n\nE.g. https://godbolt.org/z/reddW6qe5: the null address check is simply ignored by both gcc/clang, and it also yields a helpful warning:\n\n    warning: reference cannot be bound to dereferenced null pointer in well-defined C++\n    code; pointer may be assumed to always convert to true [-Wundefined-bool-conversion]\n    \n    \nLet\u0027s make this `const skjson::ObjectValue* obj` (and update all other call sites).\n\n---\n\nCool, I see you already fixed it as I was typing this up :)  Leaving the comment in case it\u0027s informative.",
